      "writtenOn": "2024-10-11T23:57:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no restriction here that says that the partner can\u0027t implement the new API. I want them to adopt the new technology. The issue is that the function that they call here is 1.0 getDataRegistrationState which only supports the old types. A proper implementation of a 1.0 method should only return 1.0 types in HIDL.\n\nThe HIDL type system is designed to prevent exactly this case (though you see it\u0027s easy to workaround here unfortunately). The original concern is that if the value is unknown, it may be the Google value, or it may be a random other value that happens to conflict (partners may reinterpret_cast other values here, which may confuse the AOSP framework in the future). We need to continue supporting such cases in the AOSP framework for many years.\n\nIn order to return this value, it should return it via new functions that added the new types and (should) have corresponding VTS tests:\n- getDataRegistrationStateResponse_1_4\n- getDataRegistrationStateResponse_1_5\n- getDataRegistrationStateResponse_1_6\n\nas this is what the HIDL type system enforces backwards compatibility, and how the interface on all other devices should have been working until this time.",
      "parentUuid": "5a5ba104_9999cbc7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 86,
        "endChar": 9
      },
